	('034a3648-6d37-4598-8719-9f2a2b39ffd1', '1-norm Support Vector Machines', 'The standard 2-norm SVM is known for its good performance in two- In this paper, we consider the 1-norm SVM. We class classi£cation. argue that the 1-norm SVM may have some advantage over the standard 2-norm SVM, especially when there are redundant noise features. We also propose an ef£cient algorithm that computes the whole solution path of the 1-norm SVM, hence facilitates adaptive selection of the tuning parameter for the 1-norm SVM.', '{"Zhu, Ji","Rosset, Saharon","Tibshirani, Robert","Hastie, Trevor"}', '6483dd11-ae6f-4451-928b-35cd7dafba93', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2003/file/49d4b2faeb4b7b9e745775793141e2b2-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:47.500111+00', '[-0.033513755,-0.029317548,0.032824565,-0.038017087,0.009630762,0.0264664,0.03360996,0.033790242,0.027548075,0.0006992395,0.034137305,-0.03552418,0.025933111,0.011167417,0.060666163,0.033532023,0.04887519,0.04119743,-0.057159662,0.0031267486,-0.011982677,-0.029326657,0.02277017,-0.066367045,0.004028279,0.026741453,-0.012997117,-0.0832069,-0.038370665,-0.2456845,0.017522799,-0.05311235,0.06931577,-0.0075094854,-0.046661083,-0.048408706,-0.024602624,0.06584269,-0.04477068,0.053899862,0.024529876,-0.0150823835,0.008798704,-0.07628332,-0.012611073,-0.06984828,-0.006360588,-0.01912871,-0.003809374,-0.0049852915,0.015297236,-0.038566362,0.00031779724,0.0022244598,0.024328861,0.06059541,0.021874025,0.04820997,0.008251826,0.02908765,0.03568859,0.0344352,-0.16514476,0.0426623,0.034761146,-0.011614893,-0.027254405,-0.07018179,0.017685462,0.065432705,-0.029416582,0.010776035,0.023377009,7.583746e-05,0.008772468,-0.03498007,0.011788627,-0.01961133,-0.0061965277,0.03792781,0.0036550206,-0.018720588,-0.01914201,-0.05350131,-0.020668155,0.00019652414,0.0017579765,-0.040568657,0.08129293,-0.006396795,-0.03004289,-0.04248602,0.0031777842,0.06945776,-0.058148462,-0.063288294,0.0029115228,0.053831868,-0.0154084