-0.021693097,0.006928884,-0.07686048,-0.08481444,-0.051768318,-0.03402734,-0.017682469,-0.064854264,0.0051156934,-0.0065938584,-0.021785634]'),
	('088d60ef-b718-4a74-9bcb-942bfd9a0d7e', 'Risk-Averse Bayes-Adaptive Reinforcement Learning', 'In this work, we address risk-averse Bayes-adaptive reinforcement learning. We pose the problem of optimising the conditional value at risk (CVaR) of the total return in Bayes-adaptive Markov decision processes (MDPs).  We show that a policy optimising CVaR in this setting is risk-averse to both the epistemic uncertainty due to the prior distribution over MDPs, and the aleatoric uncertainty due to the inherent stochasticity of MDPs. We reformulate the problem as a two-player stochastic game and propose an approximate algorithm based on Monte Carlo tree search and Bayesian optimisation. Our experiments demonstrate that our approach significantly outperforms baseline approaches for this problem.', '{"Rigter, Marc","Lacerda, Bruno","Hawes, Nick"}', '3b78fba9-1e0e-4622-8bcd-018ea1b8d903', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2021/file/08f90c1a417155361a5c4b8d297e0d78-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:03.219852+00', '[-0.082255185,-0.0075073526,0.017034594,-0.024925606,0.0058009,0.036509726,0.055348933,0.024717398,0.088913254,0.023590231,0.046576776,-0.053042717,-0.00080504105,0.08084064,0.04061316,0.034478925,-0.03618172,0.0145041775,-0.023451703,0.0039948123,0.038471498,-0.03620356,0.018974371,-0.0739835,0.024618695,0.0006144069,-0.049365647,-0.055430412,-0.046384554,-0.2324019,0.0022579217,-0.055360157,-0.013994106,-0.054895103,-0.017365659,-0.016779216,-0.03230181,0.050855383,0.006152667,0.03926241,0.008778301,0.01938735,-0.0289819,-0.0602563,-0.03610511,-0.0755268,0.01979036,-0.034103673,-0.019610126,-0.036419638,0.014194711,-0.012833258,0.041835446,-0.0123906415,0.051645044,0.028893188,0.05183962,0.075144954,0.014391641,0.07982544,-0.015627572,0.032213476,-0.1556535,0.09030702,0.028299714,0.040714923,-0.045009006,0.001230424,0.011142433,0.030233929,-0.043627948,0.07284021,0.008103514,0.06126983,0.04874737,-0.0053621265,0.018887352,-0.05064367,