	('064f597c-fb9d-4cf3-9e87-713581c0d979', 'An Application of Tree-Structured Expectation Propagation for Channel Decoding', 'We show an application of a tree structure for approximate inference in graphical models using the expectation propagation algorithm. These approximations are typically used over graphs with short-range cycles. We demonstrate that these approximations also help in sparse graphs with long-range loops, as the ones used in coding theory to approach channel capacity. For asymptotically large sparse graph, the expectation propagation algorithm together with the tree structure yields a completely disconnected approximation to the graphical model but, for for finite-length practical sparse graphs, the tree structure approximation to the code graph provides accurate estimates for the marginal of each variable.', '{"Olmos, Pablo","Salamanca, Luis","Fuentes, Juan","Pérez-Cruz, Fernando"}', '62a3b6a3-560d-401b-bac0-fd77926acb96', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2011/file/58c54802a9fb9526cd0923353a34a7ae-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:39.682693+00', '[-0.018914158,-0.010635189,0.007514561,-0.007381008,0.06315716,0.029062206,-0.033865757,0.029162228,0.06497601,-0.00791519,0.030073425,-0.052896332,0.05555997,0.054061618,0.01676341,0.067047544,-0.011072821,0.031207174,-0.038845424,0.010966934,0.07515991,-0.04406906,0.004839733,-0.036199965,0.04048867,0.019716622,-0.0066844034,-0.048647016,-0.02598219,-0.22256663,-0.005548256,-0.038876757,0.08240234,-0.02696055,0.018502153,-0.047926,0.0013322935,0.003945231,-0.054044344,0.06102417,0.037664678,0.0102868425,-0.052695215,-0.006603984,0.007535569,-0.063826315,-0.04978216,0.021419749,-0.027382048,-0.07095835,0.015449668,-0.03217805,0.029086392,0.011588093,0.028266273,0.03018304,0.021351546,0.026223773,-0.0027910694,0.05134,0.03333923,0.055539675,-0.16057336,0.06027621,0.07640547,0.080666,-0.044669148,0.015996879,0.051783677,0.09452662,-0.019931538,0.046672285,-0.0029996827,0.058