	('0439c706-7f03-43e5-aa25-1bd52b65517d', 'Implicit Regularization of Discrete Gradient Dynamics in Linear Neural Networks', 'When optimizing over-parameterized models, such as deep neural networks, a large set of parameters can achieve zero training error. In such cases, the choice of the optimization algorithm and its respective hyper-parameters introduces biases that will lead to convergence to specific minimizers of the objective. Consequently, this choice can be considered as an implicit regularization for the training of over-parametrized models. In this work, we push this idea further by studying the discrete gradient dynamics of the training of a two-layer linear network with the least-squares loss. Using a time rescaling, we show that, with a vanishing initialization and a small enough step size, this dynamics sequentially learns the solutions of a reduced-rank regression with a gradually increasing rank.', '{"Gidel, Gauthier","Bach, Francis","Lacoste-Julien, Simon"}', '313a73ae-5a16-42d5-aba7-f6db81ba1698', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2019/file/f39ae9ff3a81f499230c4126e01f421b-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:25.083731+00', '[-0.033806056,0.014289351,0.03560906,0.012345808,-0.017687561,0.027057918,-0.014578258,0.014399824,0.05859915,-0.024293778,0.029360812,-0.041264042,0.063340984,0.0742846,0.04695636,-0.01200563,0.015190218,0.053560376,-0.07782255,0.031237166,0.008313205,-0.04264237,-0.049739383,-0.054304857,0.020109212,-0.033388544,-0.020450566,-0.024510888,-0.015618877,-0.29489425,0.07273324,-0.032140832,0.04581352,-0.025666945,0.030166851,-0.004712422,-0.014837587,0.04940928,-0.014700281,0.04407124,0.0124501195,0.038006928,0.0024432712,-0.046623554,-0.01574009,-0.016220305,-0.026370546,-0.02887029,-0.016504122,-0.0556035,0.011452207,0.0002838624,-0.0019453053,0.022851644,0.055136804,0.018832926,0.07544781,0.054529283,0.06173315,0.055255614,0.007862331,0.029083293,-0.15453705,0.04962079,0.01801623,0.046901893,-0.03