	('09bc3b86-492a-44e9-84cf-10e1fe455f63', 'Directional Hearing by the Mauthner System', 'We provide a computational description of the function of the Mau(cid:173) thner  system.  This  is  the  brainstem  circuit  which  initiates  fast(cid:173) start  escapes  in  teleost  fish  in  response  to  sounds.  Our  simula(cid:173) tions,  using  back propagation in  a  realistically  constrained  feedfor(cid:173) ward  network,  have generated hypotheses  which  are directly inter(cid:173) pretable  in  terms  of the  activity  of the  auditory  nerve  fibers,  the  principle  cells  of the  system  and  their  associated  inhibitory  neu(cid:173) rons.', '{"Guzik, Audrey","Eaton, Robert"}', 'f78e9714-be69-44be-bc21-2f3df72c09cc', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/1993/file/da8ce53cf0240070ce6c69c48cd588ee-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:53.774901+00', '[-0.075093634,-0.020756306,0.0036895901,0.037101205,-0.01320631,0.022767106,0.062008522,-0.00040750566,0.035719432,-0.0110864015,0.0097571835,-0.11032818,0.042517714,0.03568636,0.05125572,0.019231297,0.010001881,0.05075202,-0.034305997,0.033457268,0.03306634,-0.010096093,-0.054989096,-0.08121834,-0.035311706,0.034299325,-0.056939483,-0.004057067,-0.021111228,-0.23659965,0.00041843715,-0.07038411,0.055137258,-0.044524554,-0.02782453,-0.01031008,-0.01863221,0.0184463,-0.030091785,0.06340347,0.06196732,0.0562131,0.0049878233,-0.07594554,-0.037339423,-0.04019631,-0.054214757,-0.021647232,0.018049585,-0.05403867,-0.029161062,-0.03856256,0.02524833,0.034181666,0.046020906,0.01370835,0.08519151,0.057461657,0.03652023,0.044383544,0.09313665,0.031406015,-0.18627453,0.056472383,0.050776117,0.038791265,-0.014434782,0.00802492,0.03481725,0.026383866,-0.05488477,0.024534676,0.019692242,0.0066697607,0.060066946,-0.024528397,-0.008943231,-0.008912677,0.015844353,0.026499163,0.017381974,-0.047741074,-0.013451472,-0.023144117,-0.029406244,0.007909554,0.027950041,-0.08270119,-0.021725124,-0.0006716696,-0.