	('04783862-ea5c-4495-a0b4-1e87ca1e46c3', 'Deep State Space Models for Unconditional Word Generation', 'Autoregressive feedback is considered a necessity for successful unconditional text generation using stochastic sequence models. However, such feedback is known to introduce systematic biases into the training process and it obscures a principle of generation: committing to global information and forgetting local nuances. We show that a non-autoregressive deep state space model with a clear separation of global and local uncertainty can be built from only two ingredients: An independent noise source and a deterministic transition function. Recent advances on flow-based variational inference can be used to train an evidence lower-bound without resorting to annealing, auxiliary losses or similar measures. The result is a highly interpretable generative model on par with comparable auto-regressive models on the task of word generation.', '{"Schmidt, Florian","Hofmann, Thomas"}', '577342c0-5187-4d70-a0c1-4ada9d3b9f2b', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2018/file/0cd60efb5578cd967c3c23894f305800-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:25.865936+00', '[-0.005440303,-0.021656508,-0.012226298,-0.009933328,-0.003537739,0.033731155,-0.014458035,0.03438404,0.029487386,-0.022442894,0.0041670105,-0.006588815,0.057724446,0.053459078,-0.0029604044,0.0029873,-0.023044506,0.008392577,-0.050353047,-0.021538923,0.07680002,-0.018047689,0.056632083,-0.0147429705,0.0068857674,-0.026418537,-0.013839748,-0.04438854,-0.045452267,-0.26245,-0.010191467,-0.030144019,0.04056126,-0.0141432965,0.005345777,-0.0364822,-0.07893503,0.03498995,-0.0068842834,0.049461022,0.012251011,0.025043378,0.012654198,-0.011160641,-0.0076832795,-0.059899364,-0.011835869,-0.0067350077,-0.03325826,-0.0045779524,0.01594005,-0.015474462,0.017095527,0.029853733,0.053293295,0.018601192,0.05649041,0.020566389,0.043547355,0.058038395,0.0218158,0.04188487,-0.20687115,0.04617705,0.032330554,0.01639