	('0ac03ad0-8be2-4845-9e60-023dc6dc264d', 'Predictive App roaches for Choosing Hyperparameters in Gaussian Processes', 'Gaussian  Processes  are  powerful  regression  models  specified  by  parametrized mean and covariance functions.  Standard approaches  to  estimate  these  parameters  (known  by  the  name  Hyperparam(cid:173) eters)  are  Maximum  Likelihood  (ML)  and  Maximum  APosterior  (MAP)  approaches.  In this paper, we  propose and investigate pre(cid:173) dictive  approaches,  namely,  maximization  of  Geisser''s  Surrogate  Predictive Probability (GPP) and minimization of mean square er(cid:173) ror with  respect to GPP  (referred to as  Geisser''s  Predictive mean  square  Error  (GPE))  to  estimate  the  hyperparameters.  We  also  derive  results  for  the  standard  Cross-Validation  (CV)  error  and  make  a  comparison.  These approaches are tested on  a  number of  problems and experimental results show that these approaches are  strongly competitive to existing approaches.', '{"Sundararajan, S.","Keerthi, S."}', '9b744016-c818-4470-aaba-8db77de82c96', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/1999/file/e8fd4a8a5bab2b3785d794ab51fef55c-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:50.490219+00', NULL),
	('04e6559a-f777-484f-aef7-55f694276f03', 'Convergence of the Wake-Sleep Algorithm', 'The W-S (Wake-Sleep) algorithm is a simple learning rule for the models  with hidden variables.  It is  shown that this algorithm can be applied to  a factor  analysis model  which is  a linear version  of the  Helmholtz ma(cid:173) chine.  But even for a factor analysis model,  the general convergence is  not proved theoretically.  In this article, we describe the geometrical un(cid:173) derstanding of the W-S  algorithm in contrast with the EM (Expectation(cid:173) Maximization) algorithm and the em algorithm.  As the result, we prove  the convergence of the W-S  algorithm for the factor analysis model.  We  also show the condition for the convergence in general models.', '{"Ikeda, Shiro","Amari, Shun-ichi","Nakahara, Hiroyuki"}', '4223dd36-20b1-457a-bd68-a678c2e8b784', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/1998/file/0771fc6f0f4b1d7d1bb73bbbe14e0e31-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:50.83588+00', '[-0.061805837,0.02122826,0.036099736,0.031738207,0.02124202,0.06803007,0.03406238,0.028256847,0.06037372,0.0073074847,-0.01050495,-0.046202738,0.03811663,0.036264054,0.012694422,-0.005494022,0.034198064,0.029041056,-0.043448742,0.013891958,0.05759723,-0.01734004,-0.010848092,-0.032795634,0.03230662,-0.0029648512,-0.061144598,-0.019480964,-0.0076561095,-0.24512777,-0.018516308,-0.039735366,0.08275777,-0.031905666,0.00559507,-0.009685745,-0.0016515122,0.024751812,-0.025893614,0.06617726,0.019529583,0.035250917,0.0060440446,-0.05361333,-0.048342377,-0.055093624,-0.028996782,0.005816335,-0.003253711,-0.04606369,0.036269583,-0.045859247,0.017772608,0.016855845,0.039750528,0.04738803,0.016653053,0.035690945,0.015759995,0.049361974,0.004829189,0.04094192,-0.20973499,0.06222586,0.072720304,0.04122965,-0.06009659,-0.05537702,0.034951583,0.06194564,-0.05999318,0.048130102,0.002583721,0.0024022995,0.026973497,0.0018031768,0.042498846,-0.04176892,0.01049525,0.013770924,0.