	('083ce818-2f4b-402f-8469-b24c34edbd01', 'Support Vector Method for Function Approximation, Regression Estimation and Signal Processing', 'The  Support  Vector  (SV)  method  was  recently  proposed  for  es(cid:173) timating  regressions,  constructing  multidimensional  splines,  and  solving linear operator equations  [Vapnik,  1995].  In  this  presenta(cid:173) tion we report results of applying the SV method to these problems.', '{"Vapnik, Vladimir","Golowich, Steven","Smola, Alex"}', '2533af84-a66c-47f7-807e-03e421a0fe75', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/1996/file/4f284803bd0966cc24fa8683a34afc6e-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:51.951383+00', '[-0.03273396,0.023435947,0.057097185,-0.0012347773,0.077461906,-0.016058888,0.016687002,0.07325731,-0.028050745,-0.0074636075,0.05380549,-0.041697927,-0.009952388,0.025292352,0.04003177,0.0020346935,0.026223643,0.07560883,-0.037754625,-0.007171156,0.018293375,-0.029224409,-0.025153214,-0.08576268,0.03352565,0.02374284,-0.05860317,-0.07058017,-0.0040374584,-0.22871526,0.01937524,-0.044871293,0.066166796,0.022917978,0.0048433132,0.017651236,0.007769899,0.047879163,-0.04617206,0.022984643,-0.0043645333,-0.030935032,-0.030575467,-0.04441806,-0.043558095,-0.040361673,-0.011250046,-0.04696231,-0.005661029,0.0062317536,0.010492689,-0.00640784,0.01927567,0.011881959,0.029380081,0.036061037,0.034689564,0.012235408,0.020368854,0.035897896,0.030052746,-0.012407514,-0.20670336,0.08272595,0.043244913,-0.00016997561,-0.033722248,-0.01296548,0.0002863754,0.0772663,-0.040549304,0.016475374,0.016743425,-0.008114109,0.0095908465,0.026334628,0.03130904,-0.0141195385,-0.039162286,0.0021357092,0.049835484,-0.019276734,-0.031039892,0.0037391682,-0.014050713,-0.030361468,0.03317546,-0.058025837,0.07003811,-0.03321806,-0.024244398,-0.010539758,-0.0074294414,0.014133048,-0.07375727,-0.064934045,0.05805315,0.012561007,-0.024733359,0.20323154,-0.0013704858,0.012422509,0.08149998,-0.043093774,0.008933875,-0.0147