	('0723959f-6117-42cc-bad9-b72b57d8b4cf', 'Hidden Markov Model of Cortical Synaptic Plasticity: Derivation of the Learning Rule', 'Cortical synaptic plasticity depends on the relative timing of pre- and postsynaptic spikes and also on the temporal pattern of presynaptic spikes and of postsynaptic spikes. We study the hypothesis that cortical synap- tic plasticity does not associate individual spikes, but rather whole ﬁr- ing episodes, and depends only on when these episodes start and how long they last, but as little as possible on the timing of individual spikes. Here we present the mathematical background for such a study. Stan- dard methods from hidden Markov models are used to deﬁne what “ﬁr- ing episodes” are. Estimating the probability of being in such an episode requires not only the knowledge of past spikes, but also of future spikes. We show how to construct a causal learning rule, which depends only on past spikes, but associates pre- and postsynaptic ﬁring episodes as if it also knew future spikes. We also show that this learning rule agrees with some features of synaptic plasticity in superﬁcial layers of rat visual cortex (Froemke and Dan, Nature 416:433, 2002).', '{"Eisele, Michael","Miller, Kenneth"}', 'e855df86-2848-4c42-817f-8a2ea142ea50', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2002/file/38651c4450f87348fcbe1f992746a954-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:48.224495+00', '[-0.0444604,0.0033781764,0.044475604,-0.03075329,-0.018437235,0.051114872,0.112305894,-0.005385539,0.06461703,-0.04285862,0.038809735,-0.048664674,0.0689016,0.10253959,-0.0027361952,0.041554976,-0.01151909,0.023258686,-0.008883869,-0.0052432613,0.027502982,-0.049801305,-0.027213514,-0.015214779,-0.006570221,0.008184971,-0.042168584,-0.058499493,-0.018172843,-0.26692274,0.0072599812,-0.030351963,0.030724335,-0.046878345,0.030075869,-0.046765752,-0.062785454,0.08608997,-0.0049685533,0.052066255,0.021368379,0.04747734,0.009472918,-0.11344256,-0.060353287,-0.0342