	('0a1ce80b-9175-4b01-8454-a50e2221f80d', 'Computing with Finite and Infinite Networks', 'Using  statistical mechanics  results, I calculate learning curves  (average  generalization error) for Gaussian processes  (GPs)  and Bayesian  neural  networks  (NNs) used for regression.  Applying the results to learning a  teacher defined by a two-layer network, I can  directly compare GP and  Bayesian NN learning. I find that a GP in general requires CJ (d S )-training  examples  to  learn  input features  of order  s  (d  is  the  input dimension),  whereas  a  NN  can  learn  the  task  with  order  the  number of adjustable  weights training examples.  Since a GP can be considered as  an  infinite  NN, the results show that even  in the Bayesian approach, it is important  to limit the complexity of the learning machine.  The theoretical findings  are confirmed in simulations with analytical GP learning and a NN mean  field algorithm.', '{"Winther, Ole"}', '6134c809-0bc1-41a9-82e1-2935c6f2ea78', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2000/file/8562ae5e286544710b2e7ebe9858833b-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:49.803687+00', '[-0.035554174,-0.017955085,0.02583167,-0.01045948,0.019291533,0.03984943,0.044644207,0.027480107,0.019624796,-0.020129366,0.012873769,-0.032234874,0.00909812,0.07520591,0.02595894,0.0026673,0.0017127328,0.048215747,-0.054816145,-0.016315293,0.030805446,-0.025799835,-0.0041351523,-0.053040627,0.014559271,0.019150522,-0.03643745,-0.03593658,-0.021386713,-0.22416806,0.013783734,-0.074394226,0.044297628,-0.004970716,-0.02422909,-0.0013678931,-0.01381985,0.06000651,0.0020696537,0.041648053,0.031736832,0.016145347,-0.033336602,-0.016540471,0.044861298,-0.02094624,4.5736357e-05,-0.031006092,-0.060981832,-0.06564815,0.009185171,-0.021974899,-0.005325887,0.032406222,0.016388064,0.05011397,0.03506501,0.06205273,0.031691257,0.064845785,-0.019225067,0.040805966,-0.19962905,0.08067629,0.04497942,0.044128876,-0.043773454,-0.013799848,-0.0