	('09799f52-21dc-4304-b03a-905c1f78128d', '488 Solutions to the XOR Problem', 'A  globally convergent homotopy method is  defined  that is capable  of sequentially producing large numbers of stationary points of the  multi-layer perceptron  mean-squared error  surface.  Using  this  al(cid:173) gorithm large subsets of the stationary points of two test problems  are  found.  It is  shown  empirically that  the  MLP  neural  network  appears  to  have  an  extreme  ratio  of saddle  points  compared  to  local  minima,  and  that  even  small neural  network  problems  have  extremely large numbers of solutions.', '{"Coetzee, Frans","Stonick, Virginia"}', '2533af84-a66c-47f7-807e-03e421a0fe75', 'submitted', 'https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/1996/file/a51fb975227d6640e4fe47854476d133-Paper.pdf', NULL, '2025-02-14 14:40:52.365843+00', '[-0.072986595,-0.041142505,0.052889567,-0.0244068,0.002456966,0.02767179,0.033810206,0.031594202,0.051304355,-0.043810446,0.010402567,-0.04423106,0.055445075,0.08314006,-0.0065268595,0.04242424,-0.00093675964,0.03609207,-0.009627686,0.0575039,0.016311705,-0.0154716335,-0.04285343,-0.0563479,0.012421335,0.0066540674,-0.03387092,-0.04989156,-0.015234625,-0.27960294,0.021832895,-0.041257713,0.083102696,-0.009576554,0.0164187,0.006984414,-0.009773038,0.042018015,0.0010873693,0.030846797,0.028450074,-0.008506888,-0.022055613,-0.09041588,0.01539743,-0.020976555,-0.053534433,-0.013959384,-0.01379263,-0.064945765,0.029667582,-0.034759328,0.038954865,-0.02563924,0.03207372,0.02924746,0.02290288,0.0463837,-0.0005661559,0.036805853,-0.011940926,0.07092953,-0.19929384,0.071004525,0.033878483,0.050878514,-0.027136633,-0.0021979602,-0.012180537,0.08366546,-0.023452617,0.013045303,0.018460091,0.041617516,0.017802311,-0.0065382086,-0.017499562,-0.02172819,-0.013070346,0.014294361,0.017140444,-0.02102613,-0.03333841,-0.040029738,-0.0059796576,-0.016547844,0.0131785255,-0.039478146,0.026696341,-0.0066685197,0.0011700502,0.0021386335,0.0023